WEBVTT

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.800
So, today is...

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.540
the 15th.

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:19.090
Mom?

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:20.790
Don't burn the fried eggs.

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:22.500
I know, I know.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:24.470
Let's see...

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:25.730
Good morning.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:26.360
Morning.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:27.710
Morning, Sou-kun

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.290
How are you feeling?

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:32.530
You could at least take today off, you know.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:35.170
Oh, I'm all right.

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:37.040
It's not so bad that I need to stay home.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.180
Are you sure?

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.810
You escaped by a hairsbreadth, right?

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:43.480
I'm just glad that it didn't end up being serious.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:44.340
Right...

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.160
Uh, but I don't remember much from when it happened.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:54.070
Sou-kun?

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:54.660
Huh?

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.360
What's wrong?

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:58.660
Maybe you really aren't well somehow...

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:02.200
Oh, no, I was just lost in thought.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:03.360
Okay.

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:28.320
Say, Kaori.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:32.280
Um, so...

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:35.030
I love you, Sou-kun.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:37.410
Uh...

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:39.170
Nah, it's nothing.

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:53.300
Morning!

00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:55.160
Morning, Airi-chan.

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:55.940
Hey.

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:58.020
Oh, hey, did you see the news?

00:01:58.020 --> 00:01:59.680
The news? About what?

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:04.180
The people with Uchihama syndrome have apparently woken up.

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:04.980
And I mean, all of them.

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:07.090
Huh? Why now?

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:07.960
No idea.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:10.180
So that means the people
from our academy too?

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:11.110
Probably.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:14.820
Thing is, a couple of them have apparently been saying weird things.

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:17.620
Like how they saw a ghost
right before they fell unconscious.

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:17.870
What?!

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:19.000
A ghost?

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:23.200
You know, just like Azuma Yaeko-san,
one of the eyewitnesses from that ghost incident.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.710
B-B-But that was a prank by the Film Society.

00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:29.510
Maybe their memories are jumbled because they just woke up.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:30.420
Could be.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:32.500
But just maybe...

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:35.620
Wouldn't be interesting if there was some causal link between them?

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:38.340
I forget, did you have an interest in the occult?

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:41.650
Nah. I'm just messing with Kaori
because she freaks out about this stuff.

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:42.930
Airi-chan...

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:54.390
I bought another new one!

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:56.210
Again? How many does that make?

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:57.030
Eight.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:59.300
Eight? What are you, stupid?

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.560
Morning, guys.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:01.950
Hey, man.
Hey, Sou!

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:01.970
Hey, Sou!

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:06.000
You okay? I heard that you got run over by a bus yesterday.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.120
No, it wasn't that bad.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:10.560
What? Were you seriously in that accident yesterday?

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:11.000
Yeah, for real. But my injuries weren't that big a deal.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.720
Were you with him too?

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:15.720
No, I was in the club room.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:19.110
When I rushed over,
Sou-kun was being treated in an ambulance.

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:20.090
I was so shocked.

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:23.480
Becoming a widow at your age would be rough.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:24.810
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:27.540
Sou-kun and I are just childhood friends, okay?

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.060
What? For real?

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:46.790
Oh, there you are, Sou-kun.

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:48.080
Hey, Sou!

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:50.370
Sou, were you able to buy that red bean bun?

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:51.250
Yeah.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:52.540
I see that you're all here.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:54.720
We're all here!

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:57.000
All members...

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:59.130
What's wrong, Kenny-san?

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:02.340
Uh...

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:06.100
This is... all of us, right?

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:19.220
Sorry. Looks like I got mixed up.

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:20.780
Let's eat, let's eat!

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:25.530
Such nice weather.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:29.290
Seriously, days like this
make me want to go on a picnic.

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:30.660
Hey, Sou.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:31.560
Huh?

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:34.070
Didn't we have a conversation
like this before too?

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:35.120
Must be déjà vu.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:35.750
What?

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:40.520
Cases of déjà vu are memories from another world
that might have really happened.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:43.090
Or so it's been theorized by some, I hear.

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:47.600
In that world, I wonder if there's a me
who's living her life differently

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:49.720
than the one I'm living now.

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:52.130
You never know. You might already be married!

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:53.600
No way.

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:56.810
Got it!

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:02.770
We're back.

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:04.180
How'd it go?

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:07.030
We were able to borrow some partitions, desks, and chairs.

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:08.530
Good job.

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:10.320
Kaori, what about the outfits?

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:12.290
Just a little more and they'll be done.

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:13.110
Oh?

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:14.040
What's wrong?

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:18.790
There are four sets of outfits for the school festival.

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:21.860
Why did I make <i>four</i> of them?

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:23.910
Well, it's fine, isn't it?

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:26.040
We've got five members, after all.

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:26.760
What?

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:27.940
No...

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:31.180
Uh, my grandpa's forbidden me from cross-dressing, so...

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:32.300
Really?

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:35.190
Might I take a minute of your time?

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:37.730
Oh, Miss Vice President,

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:39.440
come with yet another messy problem?

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:40.710
No.

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:42.900
Today, I've only come to deliver
some lost property.

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:44.480
Lost property?

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:47.140
They said these were found
on the ground near the bus stop.

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:48.780
So they were delivered to the school.

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:50.120
The bus stop?

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:52.790
Yes, a photo and a badge, apparently.

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:54.530
So I made sure to return them to you.

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:55.040
Oh, thanks.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:55.910
Well, then, please excuse me.

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:56.790
Thank you.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:05.040
Everyone has their own badges...

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:06.160
Right?

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:07.780
Yeah, I have mine.
I do.
Yes.
I have mine.

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:12.390
This is the photo we took in the courtyard
the other day, right?

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:16.480
Oh, someone suddenly suggested that we take a group picture, and...

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:18.020
Who was it again?

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:19.960
Huh? Oh...

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:21.940
Yeah... who <i>was</i> it?

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.760
What's up with all of you today?

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:28.410
You've been acting weird since lunch.

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:33.270
It's like there's one more member that we don't know about.

00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:35.150
I've heard of clubs having ghost members,
but this is next level.

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:35.870
Knock it off.

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:37.920
It's as if just for one night,

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:41.130
we also succumbed to Uchihama syndrome.

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:43.860
Oh, not you too, Nagisa-san.

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:52.350
Kaori.

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:55.260
You know...

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:57.980
About yesterday...

00:06:57.980 --> 00:06:59.100
Do you remember?

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:01.640
Like there's any way I could forget,

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:03.600
after you rejected me so decisively.

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:04.870
Oh, uh, sorry.

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:07.520
It's just that everyone's been weird today, so I figured...

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:08.490
Honestly!

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:12.200
But I think this is for the best.

00:07:13.230 --> 00:07:15.190
I don't really know why,

00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:18.710
but I feel like I've arrived at an answer that has long eluded me.

00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:23.790
I feel like I can finally move forward now.

00:07:24.140 --> 00:07:25.250
Kaori...

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:28.820
Ah, that feels better.

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:31.800
And in any case, I'm glad that the reason you rejected me

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:34.180
was because you could only see me
as your childhood friend.

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:35.340
Yeah...

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:38.850
That's what I said, right?

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:41.430
What? You don't remember?

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:44.600
The truth is, I'm kinda drawing a blank.

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:46.500
You make the rejection feel so empty now.

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:47.660
Uh, sorry.

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:49.750
If...

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:52.280
ten years pass, or twenty years pass,

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:55.000
and you still haven't found someone you love,

00:07:55.000 --> 00:08:00.040
I'll step up to be considered again... maybe.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:01.520
O-Okay.

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:05.570
For now, getting to see you again
tomorrow is enough.

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:06.300
Yeah.

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:11.080
All right!

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:12.580
It's finished!

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:13.070
Woohoo!

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:15.350
Now we just wait to go live tomorrow.

00:08:15.670 --> 00:08:19.480
Then I'll go take the stuff in the hallway upstairs.

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:20.560
Please do.

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:29.100
Owowow... My back...

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:30.670
Look at all this.

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:33.570
That's...

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:41.620
Again...

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:44.260
with the déjà vu.

00:08:53.770 --> 00:08:54.800
I'll come again.

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:02.660
Airi.

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:10.660
That's the experimental data on Yui so far, right?

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:11.760
Are you sure?

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:12.740
Yeah.

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:13.700
There's no need.

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:18.620
Yui wasn't able to save Kaori in our timeline.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:22.580
Aren't we just living the same time over and over?

00:09:22.900 --> 00:09:23.810
Maybe.

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:26.640
But the behavior of the Yui we met

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:29.760
was hardly that of a Yui
trying to save Kaori for the first time.

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:32.700
It's doubtful that she's doing
the same thing over and over.

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:36.290
The world is continually changing.

00:09:36.290 --> 00:09:40.160
It's unthinkable that only one conclusion exists.

00:09:41.090 --> 00:09:44.420
Maybe that's just what you want to believe.

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:50.860
Hey, Sou.

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:54.380
Do you really think that Yui will succeed?

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:55.650
I don't know.

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:57.710
And even if she were to succeed,

00:09:57.710 --> 00:10:00.370
I can't be sure whether it would affect our world or not.

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:05.710
The theory that the diverged worlds will
merge back together is itself uncorroborated.

00:10:05.710 --> 00:10:07.310
Which is to say, in other words,

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:11.810
that what we're doing might be meaningless?

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:13.840
Maybe.

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:18.530
You made Yui based on such uncertain speculation?

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:21.100
What is that girl to you?

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:24.210
Is she... just a tool?

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:33.190
Do you suppose Yui knows that she'll disappear once she's carried out her mission?

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:35.320
Probably.

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:36.770
I see.

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:40.200
If you sent her off with that knowledge,

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:42.530
that was awfully cruel of you.

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:57.490
All right!

00:10:57.490 --> 00:10:59.260
Now let's give this everything we've got!

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:00.760
Yeah!

00:11:06.710 --> 00:11:09.020
Hey there! Thank you all for coming!

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:10.910
Karin-chan!

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:35.020
Okay, please write your name here.

00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:41.060
The four stars that form Andromeda's head
and Pegasus's torso:

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:46.880
Scheat, Alpheratz, Algenib, and Markab.

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:49.180
Connect these four
and you can see the Square of Pegasus.

00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:51.970
And if you look far down from there...

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:55.670
The star that shines noticeably more brightly is Fomalhaut.

00:13:00.820 --> 00:13:04.480
Fomalhaut is called the "Lonely Star of Autumn"

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:07.680
and is a first-magnitude star,
the brightest in Piscis Austrinus.

00:13:08.150 --> 00:13:10.320
The name comes from an Arabian phrase
that means "the mouth of the Southern Fish."

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:11.230
Huh?

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:12.600
The name comes from an Arabian phrase
that means "the mouth of the Southern Fish."

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:13.510
What is this?

00:13:19.070 --> 00:13:20.980
Events held on school grounds

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:24.740
will be ending at 5pm.

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:28.460
Following that, we will be holding a closing party,

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:30.750
so we hope that you will all attend.

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:34.120
Good job, everyone!

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:35.750
Good job!

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:41.000
But man, we sure ran out
of sweets fast, didn't we?

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:44.340
We were ready to close up
by just past two, after all.

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:46.890
And there was also
that thing with Kaori-san.

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:50.850
Please write your name here.

00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:53.310
Oh, there she is.

00:13:55.260 --> 00:13:57.080
I have located Sasaki Kaori-san.

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:59.680
Understood. Courteously escort her over here.

00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:01.150
Roger.

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:05.050
Excuse me. I'm a member of the
school festival executive committee.

00:14:05.050 --> 00:14:07.640
I apologize for the inconvenience,
but I need you to come with me.

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:08.370
Huh?!

00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:11.080
Wait! Wh-Where are you going?!
What? What?!

00:14:11.590 --> 00:14:14.260
This year's Miss Uchihama Academy is...

00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:15.650
Sasaki Kaori-san!

00:14:15.650 --> 00:14:16.330
Huh?

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:17.380
Sasaki Kaori-san!

00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:24.880
This should raise the standing of the Astronomy Club
one more notch within the academy, huh, Prez?

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:28.370
Yes, we're one step closer
to becoming the most powerful club!

00:14:28.370 --> 00:14:29.650
None of this makes any sense.

00:14:29.650 --> 00:14:31.220
We're supposed to be the <i>Astronomy</i> Club.

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:34.530
No one was even looking at the planetarium, you know.

00:14:36.990 --> 00:14:37.730
Yes?

00:14:39.550 --> 00:14:41.730
Oh, um...

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:47.180
Please excuse me.

00:14:47.180 --> 00:14:50.020
Oh, girl, don't do that to us!

00:14:50.020 --> 00:14:52.530
You're Fukasawa Karin-san, right?

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:54.440
Good job with your concert!

00:14:54.440 --> 00:14:56.520
You've come all this way already.

00:14:56.520 --> 00:14:58.870
Have some tea at least.

00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:00.870
Uh, okay.

00:15:02.010 --> 00:15:03.340
Here you are.

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:06.800
Tea made by Miss Uchihama herself?!

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:08.340
This is too rare an honor!

00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:11.340
Aren't you an actual pop star?

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:12.300
So?

00:15:12.700 --> 00:15:15.750
You came here because you wanted to see us about something, right?

00:15:15.750 --> 00:15:17.670
Oh, uh, yes.

00:15:17.670 --> 00:15:19.910
Could it be that you want to join the club?

00:15:19.910 --> 00:15:21.800
To give us a power boost?
Sold-out events?!

00:15:21.800 --> 00:15:23.440
That's awesome, Prez!

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:24.860
One step closer to the top!

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:25.280
Uh, uh, uh, um... Uh, um...

00:15:25.280 --> 00:15:26.980
Yeah!

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:29.400
Don't try to railroad her into joining.

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:30.370
Darn.
Darn.

00:15:30.890 --> 00:15:33.140
You actually came here
about something else, right?

00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:35.980
Uh, yes, that's right. That's right.

00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:38.870
Um...

00:15:40.510 --> 00:15:44.790
The truth is, I wasn't sure if I should talk to you about this or not.

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:47.490
About my friend—

00:15:48.140 --> 00:15:51.630
or at least, I <i>think</i>
she was probably my friend.

00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:55.640
I don't even really
understand it myself, but...

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:57.770
It was about four days ago.

00:15:58.150 --> 00:16:00.230
The fifteenth, I think.

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:01.760
I mean, seriously, it's hilarious, you know?

00:16:01.760 --> 00:16:02.930
Morning!
I mean, seriously, it's hilarious, you know?

00:16:02.930 --> 00:16:04.480
Morning.
Oh, morning, Karin.

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:08.400
There we go.

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:10.340
Oh, she's not here yet.

00:16:10.340 --> 00:16:11.940
Weird. She's always early.

00:16:11.940 --> 00:16:12.950
"She"?

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:15.000
You know, the transfer student...

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:15.910
That girl.

00:16:16.360 --> 00:16:17.270
Who?

00:16:17.270 --> 00:16:19.330
Uh, well...

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:23.660
Karin, my dear, the exhaustion must really be getting to you.

00:16:23.660 --> 00:16:24.400
Huh?

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:26.590
Yeah, I guess so.

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:31.090
But that was the only day that
I recalled something like that.

00:16:31.460 --> 00:16:33.510
And it was partly because I was busy,

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:36.700
but then I managed to forget even that.

00:16:42.440 --> 00:16:44.600
Well, we're counting on you, Fukasawa-san.

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:45.460
Yes, ma'am!

00:16:45.460 --> 00:16:48.400
Man, I'm uber-nervous!

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:50.800
Karin, think of the audience as potatoes.

00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:52.170
Potatoes?

00:16:52.170 --> 00:16:54.660
You don't get nervous around potatoes, right?

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:56.160
Those! And these!

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:58.160
And all of them! They're potatoes!

00:16:58.850 --> 00:16:59.410
Huh?

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:01.600
Hey, if you're up for—

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:05.460
Karin, it's almost time.

00:17:09.910 --> 00:17:11.040
She's not there.

00:17:15.470 --> 00:17:21.040
In that moment, I was positively certain that she existed.

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:24.550
But now I'm not so sure.

00:17:24.550 --> 00:17:28.110
No one remembers her, and there's no evidence that she was ever here.

00:17:28.620 --> 00:17:33.620
But I just had this vague feeling that I should tell you all.

00:17:34.580 --> 00:17:36.110
Why us?

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:43.150
I don't remember when, but she said that
she was glad she joined the Astronomy Club.

00:17:55.120 --> 00:17:59.280
Students are requested to leave the school as soon as they have finished cleaning.

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:02.350
Oversized trash will be collected tomorrow.

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:05.520
Well, I'm going to head home now.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:06.850
I'll leave the rest to you.

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:07.390
O-Okay. Thank you for your hard work.

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:08.470
See you tomorrow.
Goodbye.

00:18:08.470 --> 00:18:09.170
O-Okay. Thank you for your hard work.

00:18:09.170 --> 00:18:10.640
Thanks for the help.

00:18:11.510 --> 00:18:12.880
Oh, crap.

00:18:12.880 --> 00:18:16.360
I have to go submit our report
for the Student Council.

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:20.520
Oh, I have to help my class dismantle things.

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:22.120
Sorry, Sou.

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:23.560
It's fine.

00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:25.300
I'll take care of the rest.

00:18:25.300 --> 00:18:27.990
I'm just going to head home once I'm done.

00:18:27.990 --> 00:18:29.480
Okay, got it.

00:18:43.000 --> 00:18:44.190
Sou-kun.

00:18:45.660 --> 00:18:48.080
I'm going to go see how our class is doing, too.

00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:48.980
Sure.

00:18:49.550 --> 00:18:51.440
I'll wait for you at the entrance.

00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:01.330
I originally made Yui
because I wanted to save Kaori.

00:19:02.170 --> 00:19:05.450
But I suspect that that wasn't necessarily the only reason.

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:07.330
What do you mean?

00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:16.760
If the worlds are to merge back together,

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:19.960
they must be influencing each other
in some way to make it happen.

00:19:19.960 --> 00:19:21.380
I see.

00:19:21.380 --> 00:19:24.220
Because the brain is a
quantum Turing machine, right?

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:26.640
People's psyches may diverge,

00:19:27.370 --> 00:19:29.100
but they must remain linked.

00:19:34.850 --> 00:19:39.740
Then, even if Yui were to succeed
and Kaori's accident were to be prevented...

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:41.340
Yeah.

00:19:42.090 --> 00:19:44.560
It might be far further in the future than this.

00:19:45.230 --> 00:19:46.240
But...

00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:50.140
I'm sure that one day I will make Yui.

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:53.080
Why?

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:54.130
Well, because...

00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:57.040
I'm sure I'd want to see her again.

00:19:58.480 --> 00:19:59.970
Sou...

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:11.810
Nagisa-senpai!

00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:13.630
How is Kaori?!

00:20:15.160 --> 00:20:17.270
She's waiting inside.

00:20:21.230 --> 00:20:22.220
Airi-san.

00:20:23.390 --> 00:20:24.950
Let them be alone for now.

00:20:32.950 --> 00:20:34.060
Kaori...

00:20:36.480 --> 00:20:38.210
Sou-kun...

00:20:38.700 --> 00:20:39.710
Kaori.

00:20:40.330 --> 00:20:45.210
I feel like I've been dreaming this whole time.

00:20:45.210 --> 00:20:46.060
Dreaming?

00:20:46.620 --> 00:20:47.720
About what?

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:51.840
The two of us are walking
on our way home from school.

00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:55.580
I don't remember what we were talking about,

00:20:56.490 --> 00:20:58.700
but at the end, I say...

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:00.340
What do you say?

00:21:00.740 --> 00:21:04.240
I say, "I'll see you again tomorrow, right?"

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:13.330
And we finally did, Sou-kun.

00:21:13.840 --> 00:21:16.210
You took way too long, you dummy!

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:32.290
Are you serious?

00:21:32.290 --> 00:21:32.980
Yes.

00:21:33.820 --> 00:21:34.990
I see.

00:21:35.790 --> 00:21:38.630
All right. Try your best.

00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:41.480
I'll do everything I can to support you, too.

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:42.660
Yes, sir.
